{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Enable transfers to Network Printer}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Enable_transfers_to_Network_Printer}
\pard\keepn \fs36 Enable transfers to Network Printer
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This check-box is found on the \uldb Network Printer Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Network_Printer_Tab}, and allows access to a number of additional formatting options when transferring Images to a network printer.
\par 
\par As soon as this option is enabled, the Image Archive program logs into the Remote Network Printer automatically. This link remains active until the user logs-out from the printer using the \uldb Log-out button\plain\fs24 {\v EE4OAC}, or until the Image Archive application closes.
\par 
\par When transferring images to the printer using the \uldb Transfer button\plain\fs24 {\v B8__3Z}, the settings on the \uldb Network Printer Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Network_Printer_Tab} are first sent to the printer.
\par \pard 
\par All Image files that are sent to the Network printer will have their \uldb archive attribute \plain\fs24 {\v 1MP7OUG} cleared, this allows the Image Archive program to identify which files will be transferred to the printer during the next transfer session. This selection option however can be overridden by using the \uldb Include Files Already Transferred\plain\fs24 {\v Include_Files_Already_Transferred} check-box on the \uldb Image File Source Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Source_Tab}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Errors Help}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Errors_Help}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Cancel Image Transfer}
\fs36 Errors Help
\par \pard \fs24 
\par During an FTP session, there are numerous operations that can result in an error code being generated either by the local PC or the remote computer. The PC uses as 'Windows Sockets' interface to implement its FTP transfers. Consult the following list of error codes as to why the particular function failed to complete.
\par 
\par Error codes will usually be recorded in the \uldb log file\plain\fs24 {\v User_Log_File}, displayed in the Archived Images List and/or displayed in the \uldb status display bar\plain\fs24 {\v The_Status_Bar}
\par \pard 
\par \i\ul Hint :\plain\i\fs24  The easiest way to reset an error condition is to \uldb logout\plain\i\fs24 {\v EE4OAC} followed again by a \uldb login\plain\i\fs24 {\v 5P5S_OV} to restart the FTP connection.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \fs28 FTP Error Codes\fs36 
\par \pard\tx4635 \fs24 
