{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Exclude Button}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Exclude_Button}
\pard\keepn \fs36 Exclude Button
\par \pard \fs24 
\par The Exclude button on the \uldb Image File Source Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Source_Tab} is used to temporarily exclude the selected files from being included in the next image transfer option. 
\par 
\par This exclusion does not alter the selected files in any way, and is cleared when the \uldb Refresh button\plain\fs24 {\v Refresh_button} is pressed.
\par 
\par A typical use for this button would be to selectively transfer a set of image files from the users Image directory.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} FTP Host}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 3H.QV4}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Change Dir}
\fs36 FTP Host
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This is the name of the Remote host computer where the \uldb FTP User account\plain\fs24 {\v 3HIUH2} exists. SEM Image files are transferred to this account.
\par 
\par If the user does not know the name of the remote computer specifically, then the internet address of the remote computer can be entered directly e.g:
\par 
\par \f2\b ftp.acme.co.uk
\par 149.23.45.52\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par Are both equally valid entries for the above imaginary internet FTP site. See your system administrator for the Internet address of the remote computer you wish to access.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} FTP Image Dir}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1BZPJX}
\pard\keepn \fs36 FTP Image Dir
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This is the path on the \uldb host computer\plain\fs24 {\v 3H.QV4} that the \uldb user account\plain\fs24 {\v 3HIUH2} exists. The SEM Image files are transferred to this directory on the remote Host computer.
\par 
\par \i\ul Note :\plain\i\fs24  By default, if the filename(s) of the SEM Image file(s) already exist on the remote computer, FTP will overwrite the Image files on the remote computer, and replace them with those most recently copied. If the filenames of the Images to be transferred are all different to those already present on the remote computer, no files will be overwritten.\plain\fs24 
\par \page
