{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Introduction}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Introduction}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Exclude Button}
\fs36 Introduction
\par \pard \fs24 
\par The LEO FTP Image Archive Utility (ImgArc) is designed to allow the SEM Operator to transfer a copy of saved \uldb SEM Image Files\plain\fs24 {\v SEM_Image_Files} to a remote computer using FTP; the TCP/IP Internet protocol for file transfer.
\par 
\par This application program assumes that the TCP/IP protocol is installed and correctly configured on the system that you are running the application on, and on your target system. Your local system administrator should be able to help you configure your computer(s) to use this protocol..
\par \pard 
\par The remote or host computer must be capable of receiving FTP commands, and should be configured as an FTP server. There is additional support for network printers that accept commands and images using the FTP protocol. Such an example is the Codonics NP1600 printer.
\par 
\par The user configures ImgArc by providing the internet address of a host computer, along with username, password and target directory that describe where the image files are to be stored.
\par 
\par A basic interface exists for the user setting up ImgArc to verify that these parameters have been set correctly prior to transferring their image files.
\par \pard 
\par When this application is invoked from the SEM user Interface, only those image files with their \uldb archive attribute\plain\fs24 {\v 1MP7OUG} set will be copied. The archive bit is cleared only when the image has successfully been copied to the host computer.
\par 
\par Finally, the user can also specifiy whether files are copied as they are saved, or at the end of a 'session' on the SEM.
\par \page
