{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} The File Copy Dialog}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 5VFV.V}
\pard\keepn \fs36 The File Copy Dialog
\par \pard \fs24 
\par When a file copy operation is in progress, a dialog similar to the one show below appears. The information displayed within it is as follows :
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Image Number : The current image being transferred from the current 'batch' as displayed in the \uldb Local Image List\plain\fs24 {\v SEM_Image_Files}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Source : The source of the current SEM Image being transferred as specified on the \uldb Source Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Source_Tab}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Destination : The target location for the image file specified on the ImgMgr \uldb Destination Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Destination_Tab}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Progress : The percentage of the current file transfer that has completed so far
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Bytes Remaining : The number of bytes waiting to be transferred to the \uldb remote host computer\plain\fs24 {\v 3H.QV4}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 During transfer, there are two command buttons that can be pressed :
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \uldb Cancel All\plain\fs24 {\v 9A3XVB}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \uldb Cancel\plain\fs24 {\v 3M0LA4C}
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \i\ul Note :\plain\i\fs24  The time taken to transfer images relies entirely on the type of connection being used between the local and remote host computers. This can vary between seconds and minutes for the same image, where connection types vary.\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} The Status Bar}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} The_Status_Bar}
\pard\keepn \fs36 The Status Bar
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This graphic provides information on the current state of the ImgArc program. All pertinent status messages are recorded in the \uldb User Log File\plain\fs24 {\v User_Log_File}. When an FTP operation is in progress, the \uldb FTP Status Bar\plain\fs24 {\v FTP_Status_Bar} reflects what action if any is currently pending.
\par 
\par Any FTP or other \uldb error codes\plain\fs24 {\v Errors_Help}/messages are also stored in the \uldb User Log File\plain\fs24 {\v User_Log_File}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} The Status Button}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} LIYTPP}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Image File Destination Tab;Image File Source Tab}
\fs36 The Status Button
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This command asks ImgArc to return the current system status from the FTP session. The resultant status string (if any) is displayed in the \uldb Status Bar\plain\fs24 {\v The_Status_Bar}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} The Transfer Button}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} B8__3Z}
\pard\keepn \fs36 The Transfer Button
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This button will be greyed out until the \uldb user\plain\fs24 {\v 3HIUH2} has \uldb logged in\plain\fs24 {\v 5P5S_OV} to the \uldb remote host computer\plain\fs24 {\v 3H.QV4}.
\par 
\par The Transfer button will action an image transfer operation using settings displayed on the \uldb Source Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Source_Tab} and \uldb Destination Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Destination_Tab}. Each event during the transfer operation is stored in the \uldb user log file\plain\fs24 {\v User_Log_File}. 
\par 
\par During the Image transfer operation a file \uldb copy progress dialog\plain\fs24 {\v 5VFV.V} will appear showing the status of each Image file being transferred.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Update Log}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 124L4M7}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Image Transfer option}
\fs36 Update Log
\par \pard \fs24 
\par This causes the \uldb User log file\plain\fs24 {\v User_Log_File} display to be refreshed. Usually, this function is automatic and will automatically update the log file display whenever an entry is added to the log file.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} User Log File}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} User_Log_File}
\pard\keepn \fs36 User Log File
\par \pard \fs24 
\par Each event in ImgArc such as \uldb logging in\plain\fs24 {\v 5P5S_OV} and \uldb out\plain\fs24 {\v EE4OAC} of the remote\uldb  host computer\plain\fs24 {\v 3H.QV4} and transferring Image Files is recorded in a log file specified on the \uldb Options Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Options_Tab}. The User directory where the log file exists is shown on the \uldb Source Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Image_File_Source_Tab}.
\par 
\par The \uldb Options Tab\plain\fs24 {\v Options_Tab} also shows the contents of the log file. All \uldb FTP errors\plain\fs24 {\v Errors_Help} are also logged to this file.
\par \page
